  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH SSH Control Center",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA unified, non-intrusive SSH control center plugin for [DeepSeek Harness (DSH)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (`@dsh-external/dsh-ssh-control`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH SSH Control Center",
      "text": "This plugin equips DSH with **cross-platform (Linux & Windows), encoding self-healing (UTF-8 & GBK), stateless, and multi-host concurrent dispatch** capabilities. AI agents can seamlessly interact with remote Linux, NAS, Windows, and container hosts in the same session without hijacking or breaking the native local development environment.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "📸 Settings & Dashboard Preview",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "🌟 Key Features",
      "text": "- **Unified Composite Hub (`ssh_control`)**: Consolidates remote command execution, file IO, file transfer (`upload`/`download`), container inspection (`docker`), dynamic logs (`tail`), and port tunnels into a single tool, reducing Tool Schema token overhead by 85%+.\n- **Cross-Platform Dual-Dialect (Linux POSIX + Windows PowerShell)**: Automatically senses remote OS types. Uses standard POSIX syntax for Linux hosts and PowerShell commands/paths for Windows hosts.\n- **Intelligent Encoding Self-Healing (UTF-8 + GBK/CP936)**: Native multi-encoding detection and auto-transcoding for Windows Chinese systems, eliminating broken characters and garbled output.\n- **Bi-Directional File Transfer (SCP Stream)**: Supports single file and directory upload (`upload`) and download (`download`), with multi-host batch dispatch.\n- **Batch Multi-Host Concurrent Dispatch**: Natively supports comma-separated targets (e.g. `server: \"nas-server, app-node, web-cluster\"`). Powered by `Promise.all` concurrent SSH pipes for parallel batch execution and aggregated reporting.\n- **Structured Container Inspection (Docker)**: Real-time structured extraction of container states, images, ports, and health status.\n- "
    },
    {
      "section": "🌟 Key Features",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "🏛️ Architecture Overview",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "🛠️ Tool Specification (`ssh_control`)",
      "text": "| Action | Parameters | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `exec` | `server`, `command`, `workdir?`, `timeoutMs?` | Execute shell commands on single or multiple hosts in parallel (cross-platform) |\n| `read` | `server`, `path`, `offset?`, `limit?` | Read remote files bounded by lines |\n| `write` | `server`, `path`, `content` | Write remote file content via stdin stream (zero quoting loss) |\n| `upload` | `server`, `localPath`, `remotePath`, `recursive?` | Upload local file or directory to remote host(s) |\n| `download` | `server`, `remotePath`, `localPath`, `recursive?` | Download remote file or directory to local machine |\n| `tail` | `server`, `path`, `lines?`, `pattern?` | Tail end of logs with optional regex/keyword filtering |\n| `docker` | `server`, `command?` | Structured Docker container inspection or docker commands |\n| `status` | `server?` | Probe target host uptime, memory, OS, and **all disk mount watermarks** |\n| `tunnel` | `server`, `port`, `targetPort?`, `tunnelAction` | Manage background SSH port-forwarding tunnels |\n| `list` | *none* | Parse local `~/.ssh/config` to discover available SSH hosts |\n| `attach` / `detach` | `server?`, `path?` | (Optional) Bind or unbind"
    },
    {
      "section": "🛠️ Tool Specification (`ssh_control`)",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Installation",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Option A: One-click install from GitHub (prebuilt bundles included)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add github:pipipigu/dsh-ssh-control"
    },
    {
      "section": "Option B: Local development via link",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add link:/path/to/dsh-ssh-control"
    },
    {
      "section": "Launch DSH Web",
      "text": "dsh web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Scenario 1: Status & Multi-Mount Disk Watermarks",
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"status\",\n  \"server\": \"nas-server\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "section": "Scenario 2: Batch Upload to Multiple Servers",
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"upload\",\n  \"server\": \"app-node-01, app-node-02\",\n  \"localPath\": \"dist\","
    },
    {
      "section": "Scenario 3: Log Extraction with Error Filtering",
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"tail\",\n  \"server\": \"web-cluster\",\n  \"path\": \"/var/log/app.log\",\n\n---"
    },
    {
